# This sshd_config snippet integrates isshue with OpenSSH.
#
# It is commented by default so as not to interfere with the currently
# running configuration. The main OpenSSH configuration might also contain
# directives that are incompatible with the configuration below,
# and might need to be adjusted before activating it.
#
# The `ExposeAuthInfo` and `ForceCommand` directives are required.
# The `AuthenticationMethods` directive can be skipped if it is
# the same in the main configuration. Note however that isshue
# only works with `PubkeyAuthentication`. Requiring multiple
# different keys for authentication as in
#
# AuthenticationMethods publickey,publickey
#
# is also not explicitly supported.
#
# Disabling `Banner` ensures that a printed secret is not intermixed
# with a server banner presented by OpenSSH.

# Match User isshue
#   Banner none
#   ForceCommand /usr/bin/isshue
#   ExposeAuthInfo yes
#   AuthenticationMethods publickey
